{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DoublyPeriodicBoundedLocalization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DoublyPeriodicBoundedLocalization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.DoublyPeriodicLiouville"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DoublyPeriodicBoundedLocalization.bounded_of_doublyPeriodic_of_bounded_on_ball","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DoublyPeriodicBoundedLocalization.bounded_of_doublyPeriodic_of_bounded_on_ball","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DoublyPeriodicBoundedLocalization.lean#L36-L74","doc":"**Boundedness localizes to the fundamental domain.** A function `f` periodic under both\nvectors of an `ℝ`-basis `b` of `ℂ` and bounded by `C` on the closed ball of radius\n`‖b 0‖ + ‖b 1‖` (which contains a fundamental parallelepiped) is bounded by `C` everywhere:\nevery `z` is, up to a lattice translation `f` ignores, congruent to a point of that ball. ","signatureChunk":0}]}